※ pl4g-test: compile=fail
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 4479 LANG_PURE_WRITES_ELSEWHERE

※ The table taken from at the top of each turn is the one the function made
※ on the first turn and the one at the top level on every turn after: the way
※ back round the loop brings somebody else's.  So taking from it is an effect,
※ which a pure function does not have -- though when the turn is worked out the
※ way back is not there yet, which is why the question waits for the body.

let std := ⎕import("std")

let numbers: mut ⸨u8: u8⸩ = ⸨⸩

fn drained(n: u8) → u8:
    let d: mut ⸨u8: u8⸩ = ⸨⸩
    foreach i := 0u8…n:
        _ ← †d⸨i⸩
        d ← numbers
    n

@[startup]
fn main(init: std.Init) → u6:
    if drained(3u8) = 3u8: 0u6 else: 1u6
